🇺🇸🇸🇦🇵🇰🇹🇷 "Mecca Alliance" Quickly and Predictably Reveals itself as More US "Burden Sharing"

▪️The "Mecca Alliance" has recently announced mobilization against Ansarallah in Yemen as part of wider US proxy war on Iran;

▪️While Western media (and some alt media) presented the "Mecca Alliance" as Saudi Arabia, Pakistan, and Turkey (3 obedient proxies with some exceptions for Pakistan) "distancing" themselves from the US - or a reaction to US "abandonment," the alliance/pact was obviously the US extending its "Burden Sharing Network" over these nations as part of waging war on Iran and its alliance network;

▪️Ansarallah in Yemen is part of Iran's strategic depth across West Asia and US war/proxy war on the group has played out for years as the US seeks to isolate and topple Iran itself;

▪️Ansarallah's actions are a direct, defensive response to this US aggression, simply laundered through Saudi Arabia - thus the "Mecca Alliance" mobilizing against an organization defending itself from a US proxy war is simply an extension of that very US proxy war;

▪️Again, ignoring the political circus and looking only at policy papers and demonstrated networks of political capture and control, this would have been obvious from the beginning;

▪️The only question now is to what extent the "Mecca Alliance" mobilizes - while nations may be captured or influenced by the US, there is the possibility of commitments being more symbolic than substantive - as was/is the case with Egypt vs Ansarallah amid US pressure to expand its proxy war on Yemen;
